PART I — DEFINITIONS

For the purposes of this License, the following terms shall have the meanings
ascribed to them below:

"Author" means KhotJarb, the original creator and sole copyright holder of the
Software.

"Software" means the Orxis application in its entirety, including but not
limited to: all source code (frontend and backend); all user interface layouts,
component structures, and design patterns; all prompt engineering architecture,
meta-prompting structures, and instruction-generation logic; all configuration
files, environment setup, deployment scripts, and build tooling; all
documentation, written content, and marketing copy contained within the
repository; and any updates, patches, forks, or derivative works produced by
the Author.

"Output" means any custom AI instruction set, system prompt, persona definition,
or related text string that is generated by a User through their personal,
interactive use of the Software's generation feature. Outputs are produced
exclusively by the User's own inputs and exist independently of the Software's
codebase.

"Commercial Purpose" means any use, deployment, distribution, modification, or
exploitation of the Software — or any substantial portion thereof — that is
intended to generate revenue, financial compensation, or indirect economic
benefit, or that forms part of a product or service offered to third parties
for payment. This includes, without limitation: operating a hosted SaaS
platform based on the Software; white-labeling or rebranding the Software for
resale; incorporating the Software's UI/UX concepts, design system, or backend
logic into a commercial product; and sublicensing access to the Software or any
derivative thereof.

"Personal Use" means private, non-commercial use by an individual for personal
learning, skill development, local experimentation, academic study, or portfolio
review — where the Software is run solely on that individual's own hardware and
is not made accessible to third parties in any form.

